          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The purpose of this page is to explain - using appropriate mathematical terminology - Dirac’s theory of coupling particles with spin to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+field"} Yang-Mills
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+field"} gauge field
          %p We proceed in three steps: first we recall relevant facts about the gauge field itself, then we discuss charged particles in gauge fields, and finally we add spin.
          %h2#yangmills_theory Yang-Mills Theory
          %p
            (see: the main article about
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
          %p
            Under a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            we understand a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
          .un_def
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi G
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                  = succeed "," do
                    %em gauge group
                  = succeed "-invariant" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Ad
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Ad}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi κ
                        %mo :
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo ×
                        %mi 𝔤
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa: \mathfrak{g} \times \mathfrak{g} \to \R
                  on its
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
